        {
          "id": "c1-fixed-program",
          "caption": 0,
          "status": "paraphrase",
          "claim": "A Handwired program is a fixed list of arithmetic operations, mostly weighted sums and products with a ReLU, and an if statement becomes arithmetic that runs in full.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "label": "docs/README.md (what a program is)",
              "repo": "chenglou/handwired@4ea7fcb27ebe93acf49b9f29a93e162b975bad46",
              "path": "docs/README.md",
              "lines": "3",
              "quote": "a fixed list of arithmetic operations"
            },
            {
              "label": "README.md (if-else becomes matrix multiplication)",
              "repo": "chenglou/handwired@4ea7fcb27ebe93acf49b9f29a93e162b975bad46",
              "path": "README.md",
              "lines": "7",
              "quote": "Handwired transforms them into matrix multiplication + reglu over floats"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-relu-zeroes",
          "caption": 0,
          "status": "verified",
          "claim": "A ReLU is max(0, x), so it zeroes negative values.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "label": "README.md (ReLU is Math.max)",
              "repo": "chenglou/handwired@4ea7fcb27ebe93acf49b9f29a93e162b975bad46",
              "path": "README.md",
              "lines": "18",
              "quote": "Math.max(0, x) is ReLU"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-no-skip",
