          "id": "c2-minimum-formula",
          "caption": 3,
          "status": "paraphrase",
          "claim": "The minimum of a and b is a minus a ReLU of their difference, a - relu(a - b), built from rounded operations; the minus is applied to the first operand, not to the smaller one.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "label": "numeric-ui-core.ts (difference)",
              "repo": "chenglou/handwired@4ea7fcb27ebe93acf49b9f29a93e162b975bad46",
              "path": "src/runtime/numeric-ui-core.ts",
              "lines": "1943",
              "quote": "const difference = circuit.roundAffine([[a, 1], [b, -1]])"
            },
            {
              "label": "numeric-ui-core.ts (minimum is a minus a relu)",
              "repo": "chenglou/handwired@4ea7fcb27ebe93acf49b9f29a93e162b975bad46",
              "path": "src/runtime/numeric-ui-core.ts",
              "lines": "1957",
              "quote": "const result = circuit.roundAffine([[a, 1], [emitRelu(circuit, difference), -1]])"
            }
          ]
        },
